    <informations>Shelly Plus 0-10V Dimmer — mounting plate, back view.
Terminals, left to right as printed: + − S1 S2 L N.
Back view: the terminal order is mirrored against the front label face.

Official sources:
https://kb.shelly.cloud/knowledge-base/shelly-plus-0-10v-dimmer
https://kb.shelly.cloud/__attachments/a_a8004d0f11237bc2008f0b1cda40425d1dae9553eb5e7d8bf0981e825abed439/Shelly%20plus%200-10%20dimmer.jpg?cb=78b2314adab40f1111aba3f3a34abc49
https://kb.shelly.cloud/__attachments/a_f03132e84d536a3fd32f2cf59e6d5893e4e19fb188f49fd980e1406d4c0c8931/Plus-0-10V-Dimmer-internal-schematics.png?cb=32b2ce3e48de32a328a5cd89ecab9a96
https://kb.shelly.cloud/__attachments/a_d3ec94f20d065aaa858272479a3a2cca69d6bc8d0c60368ca30c2285542d6ae9/Shelly%20Plus%200-10V%20Dimmer%20multilingual%20printed%20user%20and%20safety%20guide.pdf?cb=8d1776336c57dbc0b8b0d6a89b128f78

Notes:
- Two low voltage outputs at positions0/1, blank position2, then S1/S2/L/N. Device is NOT the later PM 0/1-10V model.

Open points:
- KB explicitly labels Size HxWxD=42x37x17, unlike most standard bodies H37/W42; literal manufacturer axes are retained. Verify mechanical drawing before claiming a fabrication-accurate outline.

Nominal dimensions and an illustrative outline: corner radii, screw pitch and recesses are drawn to be recognisable, not to manufacturing CAD.</informations>
